From 22c222a855677cf3d503732bb101a7158b50ce28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:49:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HIP: kernels of mfem-mgis compiled as HIP code when MFEM uses
 HIP

With a MFEM compiled with HIP, the sources containing kernels of MFEM were
left out, and the computations by kernels refused. They are now compiled as
HIP code, so that the GPU execution mode applies to the AMD GPUs too:

- MFEMMGISDeviceCode.cmake: the HIP language is enabled with the clang of
  ROCm used by the hipcc of MFEM (CMake does not accept hipcc), on the AMD
  platform (the libraries of ROCm used by MFEM only exist there, whatever
  the variable HIP_PLATFORM), for the GPU architectures of MFEM (parsed from
  --offload-arch, required by CMake when no AMD GPU is found);
- FindMFEM.cmake: the target hip::host of ROCm gives the headers and the
  runtime of HIP to the sources compiled by the C++ compiler; the installed
  configuration finds the same ROCm;
- mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library: the behaviours for the GPU are compiled
  by the hipcc of MFEM, for its architectures (variables HIP_COMPILER,
  HIPFLAGS and HIP_PLATFORM of mfront), whatever the HIP configuration of
  TFEL;
- tests: the test executables are compiled with HIP (MFEMFieldOperationsTest
  fixed: clang refuses a narrowing conversion accepted by nvcc); the tests
  on the GPU other than the ones of --execution still use behaviours
  generated by the cuda backend, and are registered with CUDA only.

Checked with a MFEM 4.10 compiled with HIP for gfx90a (ROCm 10.1, HIP 7.16,
no AMD GPU available): mfem-mgis, its tests and the examples compile and
link, and the 213 tests of mfem-mgis and the 15 tests of the examples which
do not use a GPU pass.
